# Dour Port-Mage's trigger counts only "other creatures you control": returned to its owner's hand by Unsummon, it leaves the
# battlefield without dying, but it is not another creature, so no card is drawn (CR 603.6c, 603.10a). Its own departure is
# looked back on (a leaves-the-battlefield trigger), so only the "other" in its text keeps it from triggering.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Island
Dour Port-Mage
Unsummon
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Dour Port-Mage.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Unsummon.Cast(Dour Port-Mage)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Hand = Dour Port-Mage; Island; Island; Island; Island
